  "why": "One palette for the whole autumn set, and it is the LODGE palette plus a declared extension: the SOU-274 ticket asks for the same palette family and pixel scale as the Lodge set, so the family is imported from gen_lodge_art rather than restated, and the gate asserts the superset relation. The extension is the autumn oranges, reds and ochres the ticket asks for (16 colours, each at least 12.0 RGB units from every lodge colour). Every tile and prop in this set is quantised to exactly these colours by scripts/v3/gen_season_art.py assemble.",
  "light": "top-left (same as office-01 and the lodge): each material ramp runs dark (bottom-right faces) to light (top-left faces)",
  "daylight": "drawn in daylight colours on purpose - the renderer multiplies the outside by the season tint, which is what makes it night"
}
